## Control {{controlId}}: Provide a System Capability That Compares and Synchronizes Internal System Clocks

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization synchronizes system clocks with authoritative time sources within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant to ensure accurate audit record timestamps, managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

**Time Synchronization Architecture:**
All M365 GCC High services synchronize with Microsoft-managed NTP (Network Time Protocol) infrastructure that chains to NIST and USNO authoritative time sources:
- **Cloud Services:** Azure infrastructure automatically synchronizes all M365 service clocks with stratum-1 time sources via Windows Time Service (W32Time)
- **Audit Timestamps:** All audit records (sign-in logs, directory audits, mailbox audits) use UTC timestamps from synchronized service clocks
- **Correlation Accuracy:** Sub-second time accuracy ensures audit records from different M365 services can be correlated reliably

{{#if bitLockerEnforced}}
**Managed Endpoint Synchronization:**
{{deviceCount}} managed endpoints synchronize clocks through:
- Domain-joined devices: W32Time syncs with domain controllers, which chain to external NTP sources
- Entra ID-joined devices: Windows Time Service syncs with time.windows.com (stratum-2)
- Mobile devices: iOS/Android native NTP synchronization with carrier and platform time sources
{{/if}}

{{#if securityAlertsActive}}
**Time-Based Alert Correlation:**
Accurate timestamps enable {{securityAlertsCount}} security alert rules to correlate events across services with reliable temporal ordering.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine NTP configuration on managed endpoints, Azure time synchronization documentation, audit record timestamp accuracy, and cross-service correlation timestamp alignment.

